title: Conductor Workspace COMPLETE — embedded terminals, Symphony, shortcuts, all 4 sprints in one session
summary: All 4 Conductor workspace sprints shipped in a single session. Conductor evolved from a floating overlay to a full macOS workspace application with embedded SwiftTerm terminals running Claude Code. Multiple sessions side by side with project-specific Symphony auto-linking, keyboard shortcuts (Cmd+T/W/\/1-8), and workspace mode activation (.regular for Dock/Cmd+Tab). Apex was right about SwiftTerm — it handles Claude Code's Ink TUI flawlessly. Jinx's concerns about OSC 133 and rendering issues were not observed. The team debate was settled empirically via Sprint 0 spike. This is the single biggest Conductor evolution since its creation.
